accouplement.en:
n. The act of coupling, or the state of being coupled;
   union.
n. That which couples, as a tie or brace.

acierage.en:
n. The process of coating the surface of a metal plate (as a
   stereotype plate) with steellike iron by means of voltaic electricity;
   steeling.

adipic.en:
a. Pertaining to, or derived from, fatty or oily substances;
   -- applied to certain acids obtained from fats by the action of nitric
   acid.

agonistical.en:
a. Pertaining to violent contests, bodily or mental;
   pertaining to athletic or polemic feats; athletic; combative; hence,
   strained; unnatural.

alsikes.en:
-s form of alsike
n. A species of clover with pinkish or white flowers;
   Trifolium hybridum.

amid.en:
prep. See Amidst.
prep. In the midst or middle of; surrounded or encompassed by;
   among.

anastate.en:
n. One of a series of substances formed, in secreting cells,
   by constructive or anabolic processes, in the production of protoplasm;
   -- opposed to katastate.

androus.en:
A terminal combining form: Having a stamen or stamens;
   staminate; as, monandrous, with one stamen; polyandrous, with many
   stamens.

antimere.en:
n. One of the two halves of bilaterally symmetrical animals;
   one of any opposite symmetrical or homotypic parts in animals and
   plants.

anybody.en:
n. Any one out of an indefinite number of persons; anyone;
   any person.
n. A person of consideration or standing.

apophyge.en:
n. The small hollow curvature given to the top or bottom of
   the shaft of a column where it expands to meet the edge of the fillet;
   -- called also the scape.

appellee.en:
n. The defendant in an appeal; -- opposed to appellant.
n. The person who is appealed against, or accused of crime;
   -- opposed to appellor.

ardency.en:
n. Heat.
n. Warmth of passion or affection; ardor; vehemence;
   eagerness; as, the ardency of love or zeal.

asparaginous.en:
a. Pertaining or allied to, or resembling, asparagus;
   having shoots which are eaten like asparagus; as, asparaginous
   vegetables.

assertor.en:
n. One who asserts or avers; one who maintains or vindicates
   a claim or a right; an affirmer, supporter, or vindicator; a defender;
   an asserter.

assoilment.en:
n. Act of assoiling, or state of being assoiled;
   absolution; acquittal.
n. A soiling; defilement.

attractive.en:
a. pleasing to the eye or mind especially through beauty or charm
s. having power to arouse interest
a. having the properties of a magnet; the ability to draw or pull;

austereness.en:
n. Harshness or astringent sourness to the taste;
   acerbity.
n. Severity; strictness; austerity.

avenas.en:
plural of avena
n. A genus of grasses, including the common oat (Avena sativa);
   the oat grasses.
